5:- **Commits by workstream:** BRIEF 2eab3df; S d09ed47 (harness and v3 pre-registration); N 036bb95 (FX estimator and 4Q26 lap memos); K d4d9b6b (fee-migration residual decomposition); L 3bce8f1 (regional residual); M fe84110 (new-listing premium); P this commit (card v3, score sheet, this synthesis).
10:**Yes on the dollar target, by a margin the reader should see.** The v3 residual rule (last-quarter residual, `last_q`) with the measured mix terms beats naive "same ex-FX as last quarter" on reported dollar ADR y/y, unrounded, under both FX estimators, on both windows, with every drop-one jackknife sample below 1 (descriptive, walk-forward 1Q24-2Q26 n 10 and 2Q24-2Q26 n 9): ratio vs naive 0.916 and 0.905 under the euro fit, 0.876 and 0.871 under the baskets, 0.893 and 0.882 at the midpoint. The pre-registered criterion is met, 4 of 4 checks. Three things qualify it, and the pitch should carry all three. First, `last_q` is a post-hoc rule: it was the best line in J3's sensitivity table and was promoted to the v3 rule on 11 September before the new harness ran, with a criterion tightened for that reason (S note point 1). Second, the binding case passes by 0.011: the eur estimator on the second window has a jackknife maximum of 0.989. Third, target 2 is not an unrounded ex-FX. Reported y/y equals the disclosed integer ex-FX plus the disclosed FX effect to within 0.04 pp in every quarter, so what the dollar target removes is the charge for rounding the model, not the rounding in the data; on the integer-fair ex-FX target (target 1) the same rule is indistinguishable from naive (0.985 and 1.080, jackknife to 1.18). A reader who cares about the ex-FX sentence in the letter should use that line.
12:**Card v3 for 3Q26: reported ADR +3.4% y/y, $177.2, central band +2.0 to +4.8% ($174.8 to $179.6), on the midpoint FX estimator (-0.43 pp) that N named.** Ex-FX +3.9%. Without the K mechanics line, which is the pre-registered v3 result on its own, +3.3%, $176.9, band +1.9 to +4.6%. **4Q26: +4.2%, $174.6, central band +2.8 to +5.7% ($172.2 to $177.0); without K +3.8%, $173.9, band +2.6 to +5.0%.** The K line adds 0.17 pp in 3Q26 and, chained as K4 does it, 0.37 pp in 4Q26 (0.17 carried plus 0.20 for the 4Q26 share change), and it met its criterion by 0.003 to 0.007 of ratio, which K's own note calls a nudge rather than evidence. Both variants are in the files; the table shows both.
