30:Labels: residual and mix terms as in section 4; FX is the fitted midpoint (N, sourced from B); card v2 and H card are comparison columns (sourced from J3 and H files); harness rows descriptive. The bands are central = point plus or minus the root-sum-square of the term half-ranges (J3's convention), wide = the arithmetic sum plus the min and max of the two single FX estimators. The residual band is K's scenario table: 3Q26 mean reversion 2.40 to last_q 4.85; 4Q26 lap-only 3.06 to the K rule chained 5.22 (without K) or 3.06 to 4.85 (with K, where the K rule's 5.22 is the K line itself and is not counted twice); the K line's own band is the pre-stated coefficient range 0.000 to 0.038 (K2).
32:**GBV and revenue (comparison columns at J3's same-quarter-prior-year take rate; not inputs).** 3Q26 at 146.8mm nights (+9.9%): $26.0bn GBV, revenue $4,650mm (+13.6% y/y) with K, $4,643mm (+13.4%) without. 4Q26 at N's case B 131.8mm (+8.1%, the adopted baseline): $23.0bn, $3,134mm (+12.8%) with K, $3,123mm (+12.4%) without; at case A 132.7mm (+8.9%, the top of the band): $23.2bn, $3,155mm (+13.6%) with K, $3,144mm (+13.2%) without. A full point of 4Q26 nights is about $29mm of revenue at this ADR (the 0.9mm gap between the two cases is $21mm); a point of 4Q26 ADR is $221mm of GBV and $30mm of revenue. Both 4Q26 cases sit above the anticipated guide arithmetic of $3,050 to $3,100mm (bridge note section 7, via N) and below the Zacks consensus of $3,200mm.
