"3Q26 reported Nights and Seats Booked growth, y/y",team 9.9% (146.8mm); guide low double digits; 3Q25 denominator 133.6mm,"at or below 8.5% (at or below 144.9mm), which is 1.4 points or more below baseline and needs about 1.9mm net lost nights","at or above 10.3% (at or above 147.3mm), matching or beating 2Q26's 10.34% with the US RNPL anniversary inside the quarter",8.6% to 10.2%,"One growth point is 1.336mm nights on the fixed 3Q25 denominator. A reading inside the baseline band is consistent with either a small drag offset by the July eligibility expansion, or no drag at all, and cannot separate them.","magnitude only, not the mechanism"
"3Q26 GBV growth minus nights growth, points","2Q26 gap 5.4 pts (GBV +15.74%, nights +10.34%); 1Q26 gap 10.0 pts; 3Q25 gap 5.1 pts","gap widens to above 7 points while nights growth is at or below 9%, that is ADR and mix carrying the GBV line while nights stall",gap narrows to below 4.5 points with nights growth at or above 10%,4.5 to 7 points,"RNPL raises ADR through the mix shift to larger homes (D016, D033, D045). If RNPL cancellations are removing nights, the nights line should deteriorate faster than the GBV line, because the cancelled nights were higher-ADR than average and their removal pulls GBV down too but proportionally less once FX is stripped out. The guide already says mid-teens GBV on low double-digit nights, a gap of about 4 to 5 points, so the gap is the cleaner signal than either line alone.","a mix and cancellation composite, confounded by FX, which was a 3-point revenue tailwind in the 3Q26 guide"
"3Q26 quarter-end unearned fees, y/y","3Q25 $1,820mm. Recent path: 3Q25 +9.8%, 4Q25 +7.9%, 1Q26 +0.4%, 2Q26 -0.9%","at or below -3% y/y (below about $1,765mm). Management said RNPL produces HIGHER unearned fees in Q3 (D038), so a further deterioration means either RNPL bookings are not converting to payments, or the live unpaid base is smaller than the GBV share implies","at or above +6% y/y (about $1,930mm or more), which would show the deferred 1H26 fees arriving on schedule as payment deadlines hit, exactly as management predicted",-3% to +6%,"This is the only dated, official, directional forward prediction in the whole ledger, and it is specifically about 3Q26. The FY2025 10-K baseline seasonality says unearned fees normally FALL sequentially in Q3 as check-ins peak (D055), so the test must be y/y, not sequential. An RNPL booking creates no unearned fee at all until the guest pays (D058), so the line is a direct read on how much of the booked base is still unpaid and therefore still at risk of a payment-deadline cancellation.","payment timing, not cancellation. A weak print is consistent with deferral, with cancellation, or with a smaller live RNPL base, and cannot separate them without the unbilled-bookings balance that the 10-K says Airbnb hedges but never discloses (D056)"
"Jessie's backlog conversion, revenue over revenue plus closing unearned fees, 3Q26",3Q 2022 to 2025 constant at 69.2% to 70.3%; 2026 ran 4.0 points high in both 1Q and 2Q,"3Q26 at or above 74%, that is the 2026 wedge persisting or widening in the quarter management said it would reverse","3Q26 at 70% to 71%, back on the pre-RNPL seasonal constant",71% to 74%,Independent construction of the same payment-timing question from the level side rather than the growth side. Source: origin/jessie/backlog-conversion.,payment timing only
4Q26 nights guide issued 5 November,team 8.9% (132.7mm). PR #32 sits about 1 point below the WS10 build,"guide implies 7.5% or below. That is consistent with both the global fee and cancellation lap that PR #32 omits ex-NA, worth 0.9 to 1.8 points, and with a cancellation tail from 1H26 cohorts","guide implies 9.5% or above, which needs the tranche-2 fee ramp and the July RNPL expansion to more than cover the whole 2025 bundle lap",7.6% to 9.4%,"4Q26 is the quarter where every 2025 feature has lapped, so it is the cleanest read on underlying demand on the calendar. It is also the quarter the ledger says PR #32 is most likely to be too generous, because the cancellation redesign and fee tranche 1 were global from October 2025 and PR #32 laps them in North America only.","the combined lap, not RNPL cancellations specifically. A guide cut cannot be attributed to cancellations without management saying so"
An RNPL GBV share disclosed for 3Q26,"1Q26 roughly 20% (official), 2Q26 over 20% (call mirror only)","share flat or down versus 2Q26 while the nights line decelerates, that is adoption plateauing while the installed cancellation base keeps growing",share at or above 25% with nights growth at or above 10%,21% to 24%,The asymmetry at the centre of the hypothesis is that the gross booking uplift scales with the FLOW of new RNPL bookings in the quarter while cancellations scale with the STOCK of live RNPL bookings reaching their payment deadline. A flattening share with a still-growing stock is the configuration in which the net turns negative.,"nothing on its own. It is the variable that reconciles the funds-held read with the guide, per the EU and backlog note"
